N:HOW READ (2026-11-11): Every bar totals eight eighth units. Melody bars 1-4 use the D-natural-minor pitch set and marcato quarters; bars 5-6 hold or rest for the drop; bars 7-8 restore the hook. Bass uses repeated eighth-note roots D-F-C-A. Chord symbols give Dm-F-C-Am. Melody range D4-C5, largest leap a fifth, AB form 4+4.
N:UNCERTAIN: The cultural boundary, sound selection, degree of stylistic neutrality, accessibility of the conductor choices and originality need Indigenous, classroom and second-reader review.
